#: src/languages/json.md:10
msgid "JSONC"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/json.md:12
msgid ""
"Zed also supports a super-set of JSON called JSONC, which allows single line "
"comments (`//`) in JSON files. While editing these files you can use `cmd-/` "
"(macOS) or `ctrl-/` (Linux) to toggle comments on the current line or "
"selection."
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/json.md:15
msgid "JSONC Prettier Formatting"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/json.md:17
msgid ""
"If you use files with the `*.jsonc` extension when using `Format Document` "
"or have `format_on_save` enabled, Zed invokes Prettier as the formatter. "
"Prettier has an [outstanding issue](https://github.com/prettier/prettier/"
"issues/15956) where it will add trailing commas to files with a `jsonc` "
"extension. JSONC files which have a `.json` extension are unaffected."
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/json.md:19
msgid ""
"To workaround this behavior you can add the following to your `.prettierrc` "
"configuration file:"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/json.md:23
msgid "\"overrides\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/json.md:25
msgid "\"files\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/json.md:25
msgid "\"*.jsonc\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/json.md:26
msgid "\"options\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/json.md:27
msgid "\"parser\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/json.md:27 src/languages/json.md:60
msgid "\"json\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/json.md:28
msgid "\"trailingComma\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/json.md:28
msgid "\"none\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/json.md:35
msgid "JSON Language Server"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/json.md:37
msgid ""
"Zed automatically out of the box supports JSON Schema validation of `package."
"json` and `tsconfig.json` files, but `json-language-server` can use JSON "
"Schema definitions in project files, from the [JSON Schema Store](https://"
"www.schemastore.org) or other publicly available URLs for JSON validation."
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/json.md:39
msgid "Inline Schema Specification"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/json.md:41
msgid ""
"To specify a schema inline with your JSON files, add a `$schema` top level "
"key linking to your json schema file."
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/json.md:43
msgid ""
"For example to for a `.luarc.json` for use with [lua-language-server]"
"(https://github.com/LuaLS/lua-language-server/):"
msgstr ""

